    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the audit requirement in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the owner create handler):\n\n1. **Added an SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`** \u2014 `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`, matching the exact logger name the tests capture via `AuditLogCapture`.\n\n2. **Emitted the audit line on successful create** \u2014 placed right after `saveOwner(owner)` (so the generated `id` is populated), logging the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe line is emitted only on the successful path \u2014 it sits after all validation/rejection guards and after the save, so failed creates produce no audit line.\n\n**Test results:** The full suite passes \u2014 `Tests run: 32, Failures: 0, Errors: 0, Skipped: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`. This includes the new audit test `Cp21Tests` (which asserts an AUDIT line contains the id, customerCode, and registrationDate) and all pre-existing acceptance tests.",
